## Phase 1: Core Time Tracking App

### Core Features

#### 1. Time Tracking (Primary Experience)

**Timer Mode:**
- Persistent timer bar visible across ALL views (top navbar) -- never lose context
- One-click start/stop
- Description field, project selector, task selector, tag selector inline in the timer bar
- Running timer shows elapsed time in real-time (Stimulus controller)
- "Continue" button on past entries to restart with same project/task/tags

**Manual Mode:**
- Toggle between timer and manual entry (duration or start/end times)
- Quick-entry row at the top of the time entries list
- Inline editing of any time entry without modal popups

**Time Entry List (Day View):**
- Grouped by day with daily total
- Each entry shows: description, project (color dot), task, tags, start-end times, duration
- Inline edit on click
- Bulk actions: delete, change project, toggle billable
- "Continue" icon on each entry to restart that timer

**Weekly Timesheet View:**
- Grid: rows = project/task combinations, columns = days of the week
- Fill in hours per cell
- Row and column totals
- Save as template for recurring weeks

**Calendar View (stretch goal for Phase 1):**
- Weekly calendar with colored time blocks per project
- Drag to create new entries
- Resize to adjust duration
- Integrates visually with the project color system

#### 2. Projects & Organization

**Clients:**
- Name, contact info, notes
- Has many projects
- Used for grouping in reports

**Projects:**
- Belongs to one client (optional)
- Name, color (for visual identification across all views), billable flag
- Hourly rate (default, can be overridden per-user or per-task)
- Budget: by hours or by money, with progress tracking
- Time estimate with completion percentage
- Status: active / archived
- Architecture note for Phase 2: Include an `external_reference` field (nullable) to store Jira project key mappings

**Tasks:**
- Belong to one project
- Name, billable flag override, hourly rate override
- Status: active / done
- Architecture note for Phase 2: Include an `external_reference` field (nullable) and `external_type` enum (e.g., "jira_issue") to store Jira issue keys. Also include `external_url` for deep-linking back to the issue tracker.

**Tags:**
- Workspace-wide (not tied to a specific project)
- Name + color
- Many-to-many with time entries
- Used for cross-cutting categorization (e.g., "meeting", "code-review", "bugfix")

#### 3. Reporting

**Summary Report:**
- Group by: project, client, user, tag, or date
- Sub-group support (e.g., client -> project -> user)
- Bar chart: total hours per group (stacked billable vs non-billable)
- Pie chart: proportion by group
- Click any group to drill down into Detailed Report with that filter pre-applied
- Date range selector with presets: today, this week, last week, this month, last month, this year, custom range

**Detailed Report:**
- Line-by-line list of every time entry matching filters
- Columns: description, project, task, tags, user, date, start-end, duration, billable amount
- Sortable columns
- Pagination (server-side via Turbo Frames)

**Weekly Report:**
- Grid view: rows = grouping entity (user, project, client), columns = days
- Cell values = total hours
- Row and column totals
- Useful for team lead overview

**Report Features (all report types):**
- Filter bar: project, client, user, tag, billable status, date range
- Export: CSV, PDF (using Prawn or similar)
- Shareable via URL with encoded filters
- Print-friendly layout

**Time Recap / Dashboard:**
- Today's tracked time with breakdown by project
- This week's total vs last week comparison
- Stat cards (DaisyUI `stat` component): total hours, billable hours, billable amount, top project
- Recent activity feed
- Architecture note for Phase 2: Dashboard will show per-task time recaps (how much time spent on each Jira ticket) -- design the dashboard components to accept task-level breakdowns from the start

#### 4. User & Workspace Management

**Workspace:**
- Isolation boundary for all data
- Name, settings (default currency, week start day, time format 12h/24h)
- A user can belong to multiple workspaces

**Users:**
- Authentication (Devise or Rails 8 built-in authentication)
- Roles per workspace: owner, admin, member
- Profile: name, email, avatar, default hourly rate
- Timezone setting (all times stored in UTC, displayed in user's timezone)

**Billable Rates:**
- Workspace default rate
- Project-level override
- Task-level override
- User-level override
- Priority: task > project > user > workspace default

